"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "10", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/14"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/16"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/17"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/18"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "19", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/19"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "20", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/20"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "21", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/21"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "22", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/22"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_019_thumb.jpg", "page": "23", "label": "[19]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/23"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_020_thumb.jpg", "page": "24", "label": "[20]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/24"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "ordinance-14-november-1842", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 14 November 1842</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "9", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54016763/54016763-0013.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> Court having cognizance of the offence, on the first day of the next term thereof, to give evidence touching the said offence, and not to depart the said Court without leave: which <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12912485090865541394\"><a href=\"#12912485090865541394\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x33313\" topic=\"x33313\" title=\"Recognizance\">Recognizance</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Recognizance\"><p>“An obligation of record . . . to do some act required by law,” such as “to keep the peace, to pay a debt, or the like.” Recognizance is “somewhat like an ordinary bond, the difference being that a bond is the creation of a fresh debt, or obligation de novo...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/recognizance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, so taken, together with the Recognizance entered into by the Prisoner or Prisoners, when he she or they are admitted to Bail, shall be certified and returned to the proper Court on the first day of the next succeeding term thereof. If any such witness or witnesses shall neglect or refuse to enter into a Recognizance as aforesaid, when thereunto required, it shall be lawful for the Court to commit him her or them to jail until he she or they shall enter into such Recognizance, or be otherwise discharged by due course of law; if the Court shall neglect or refuse to bind any such Witness or Witnesses, Prisoner or Prisoners, by recognizance as aforesaid, or to return any such recognizance, when taken as aforesaid, the Court shall be deemed guilty of a misdemeanour in office, and be proceeded against accordingly.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Sec [p. 9]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> Court having cognizance of the offence, on the first day of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the next term thereof, to give evidence touching the said <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>offence, and not to depart the said Court without leave: <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>which <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4561778989001039668\"><a href=\"#4561778989001039668\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x33313\" topic=\"x33313\" title=\"Recognizance\">Recognizance</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Recognizance\"><p>“An obligation of record . . . to do some act required by law,” such as “to keep the peace, to pay a debt, or the like.” Recognizance is “somewhat like an ordinary bond, the difference being that a bond is the creation of a fresh debt, or obligation de novo...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/recognizance\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside>, so taken, together with the Recognizance <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>entered into by the Prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners,​&gt; when he &lt;​she or they are​&gt; <span class=\"deleted\">is</span> admitted to Bail, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall be certified and returned to the proper Court on the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>first day of the next succeeding term thereof. If any such <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>&lt;​witness or​&gt; witnesses shall neglect or refuse to enter into a Recognizance <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>as aforesaid, when thereunto required, it shall be lawful <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>for the Court to commit him <span class=\"deleted\">or</span> her &lt;​or them​&gt; to jail until he &lt;​&lt;​she​&gt; or <span class=\"deleted\">she</span> &lt;​they​&gt;​&gt; shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>enter into such Recognizance, or be otherwise discharged <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>by due course of law; if &lt;​the Court​&gt; <span class=\"deleted\">any Justice</span> shall neglect or refuse <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to bind any such Witness &lt;​or Witnesses,​&gt; <span class=\"deleted\">or</span> Prisoner &lt;​or Prisoners​&gt;, by recognizance as <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>aforesaid, or to return any such recognizance, when taken <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>as aforesaid, the Court shall be deemed guilty of a <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>misdemeanour in office, and be proceeded against <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>accordingly.</div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Sec [p. 9]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Nauvoo City Council Minute Book, 1841–1845", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/nauvoo-city-council-minute-book-1841-1845/125", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Ordinance, 14 November 1842, as Published in the <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Wasp</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842-as-published-in-the-wasp/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "History, 1838–1856, volume D-1 [1 August 1842–1 July 1843]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-d-1-1-august-1842-1-july-1843/58", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTit